# STE80 for Hearth docs

When you write or edit `README.md`, `docs/HISTORY.md`, or any file under
`docs/decisions/`, use **80% ASD-STE100** (Karpathy STE80). Keep hearth
tech nouns (`oMLX`, `roles.tsv`, `coding-brain`, `demand-load`).

## Do

- Short sentences. Aim ≤ 25 words (procedures ≤ 20).
- One idea per sentence. One topic per paragraph (≤ 6 sentences).
- Active voice. Imperative for steps (`Run`, `Set`, `Skip`).
- Simple tenses. Plain verbs: use, start, stop, load, set, check.
- Noun clusters ≤ 3 words (`host token file`, not longer stacks).
- Diagrams: Mermaid only (AGENTS rule 10). Prefer a table if Mermaid cannot say it.

## Do not

- AI filler: delve, leverage, tapestry, seamless, revolutionize, testament,
  beacon, cutting-edge, holistic, game-changer, robust, comprehensive.
- Passive procedure steps (`the model is loaded` → `Load the model`).
- Semicolons, Latin abbreviations (`e.g.`, `i.e.`, `etc.`), contractions in
  procedure text.
- Full ASD-STE100 dictionary enforcement — allow domain terms.
- SVG, PNG, HTML explainer pages, or Manim video in these files.

## Example

```markdown
# Bad
oMLX has been leveraged to seamlessly serve the resident role, which is
comprehensive and robust for agent workloads.

# Good
oMLX serves the resident role on `127.0.0.1:1234`.
Agents call `coding-brain` by default.
```
